# =============================================================================
# .trivyignore — Temporary Trivy suppressions
# =============================================================================
#
# Rules:
#   1. Every entry MUST have an expiration date (exp:YYYY-MM-DD).
#   2. Every entry MUST link to an upstream tracking issue/advisory.
#   3. When an entry expires, re-evaluate: remove it if the CVE is fixed,
#      or extend the date with a new justification if the fix still isn't
#      available. Never extend without re-checking upstream.
#   4. Keep the file short. A growing ignorefile is a smell.
#   5. Verify against the pinned CI Trivy (TRIVY_VERSION in security.yml /
#      cve-scan.yml) and its DB source — local `brew install trivy` uses
#      the ghcr.io DB which can classify severities differently from the
#      CI's mirror.gcr.io/aquasec/trivy-db:2.
#
# Format:
#   CVE-XXXX-XXXXX exp:YYYY-MM-DD
# =============================================================================

# CVE-2026-25680, CVE-2026-25681, CVE-2026-27136, CVE-2026-33814,
# CVE-2026-39821, CVE-2026-42502, CVE-2026-42506 — golang.org/x/net v0.49.0,
# statically linked into the pinned kubectl binary (ARG KUBECTL_VERSION in
# Dockerfile.dev; the identical v1.36.3 is fetched by
# lambda/helm-installer/Dockerfile). Surfaced by security:trivy:container-scan
# on the GCO dev image and the helm-installer Lambda image — the only two
# scanned images that carry kubectl. Fixed in x/net 0.53.0 (CVE-2026-33814)
# and 0.55.0 (the other six).
#
# Not yet clearable by a pin bump: v1.36.3 is the latest stable kubectl
# (https://dl.k8s.io/release/stable-1.36.txt) and the whole release-1.36
# branch still pins x/net v0.49.0. The bump to x/net >= 0.55.0 currently lives
# only on kubernetes master, so it lands in a future kubectl patch, not a
# release we can pull today.
#
# Low runtime risk: the flagged surfaces are not reached by kubectl acting as
# an HTTP/2 client against a trusted EKS API server — x/net/html.Render
# (CVE-2026-25680 / -25681 / -27136 / -42502 / -42506) renders HTML the client
# never produces, x/net/idna punycode (CVE-2026-39821) is off the API path,
# and the HTTP/2 SETTINGS-frame DoS (CVE-2026-33814) is a server-side parse
# while kubectl is the client. The dev image is a contributor/CI tool that is
# never deployed.
#
# Clears when a kubectl release ships with x/net >= 0.55.0: bump KUBECTL_VERSION
# in Dockerfile.dev and the pin in lambda/helm-installer/Dockerfile, then drop
# these entries. Advisory: https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-25680 (and the
# matching nvd/cve-2026-XXXXX page for each ID above).
CVE-2026-25680 exp:2026-09-22
CVE-2026-25681 exp:2026-09-22
CVE-2026-27136 exp:2026-09-22
CVE-2026-33814 exp:2026-09-22
CVE-2026-39821 exp:2026-09-22
CVE-2026-42502 exp:2026-09-22
CVE-2026-42506 exp:2026-09-22

# CVE-2026-53488, CVE-2026-53489, CVE-2026-53492 (github.com/containerd/containerd/v2
# v2.2.4) and CVE-2026-34040 (github.com/docker/docker v28.5.2 — Moby authorization
# bypass) — Go modules statically linked into the docker-buildx CLI plugin that
# Dockerfile.dev installs (ARG BUILDX_VERSION). Surfaced by security:trivy:container-scan
# on the GCO dev image — the only scanned image that carries the Buildx plugin. Fixed
# in containerd 2.2.5 / 2.3.2 and docker/docker 29.3.1.
#
# Not yet clearable by a pin bump: v0.35.0 is the latest buildx release and even buildx
# master still pins containerd v2.2.4 and docker/docker v28.5.2, so no released or
# pre-release buildx carries the fixed modules yet.
#
# Low runtime risk: buildx is a build-time CLI plugin, not a running containerd or moby
# daemon, so the containerd runtime CVEs and the Moby daemon authorization-bypass CVE are
# off the path buildx exercises (registry-to-registry image copy and BuildKit builds).
# The dev image is a contributor/CI tool that is never deployed to a cluster.
#
# Clears when a buildx release ships rebuilt against containerd >= 2.2.5 and docker/docker
# >= 29.3.1: bump BUILDX_VERSION in Dockerfile.dev (the monthly deps-scan now tracks it)
# and drop these entries. Advisory: https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-53488 (and the
# matching nvd/cve-2026-XXXXX page for each ID above).
CVE-2026-53488 exp:2026-09-22
CVE-2026-53489 exp:2026-09-22
CVE-2026-53492 exp:2026-09-22
CVE-2026-34040 exp:2026-09-22

# CVE-2026-39822 — Go standard-library os.Root symlink-following / directory
# traversal, statically linked into the docker-buildx CLI plugin installed by
# Dockerfile.dev (ARG BUILDX_VERSION, built with Go 1.26.4). Surfaced only by
# security:trivy:container-scan on the contributor/CI dev image. Fixed in Go
# 1.26.5 / 1.25.12.
#
# Every other binary this CVE used to cover has shipped a Go >= 1.26.5
# rebuild and is pinned to it: kubectl v1.36.3, helm v4.2.3, the Docker CLI
# 29.6.2, and the aws-lambda-rie in the current python:3.14 Lambda base.
#
# Not yet clearable by a pin bump: v0.35.0 is the latest Buildx release
# (v0.36.0-rc1 is prerelease-only) and is built with Go 1.26.4, so no
# released Buildx carries the fixed toolchain yet.
#
# Low runtime risk: Buildx is a local build-time CLI against a trusted
# BuildKit daemon, not deployed to a cluster, and does not traverse
# attacker-controlled filesystems via os.Root.
#
# Clears when a Buildx release ships built with Go >= 1.26.5: bump
# BUILDX_VERSION in Dockerfile.dev and drop this entry.
# Advisory: https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-39822
CVE-2026-39822 exp:2026-09-22

# GHSA-hrxh-6v49-42gf — gRPC-Go xDS RBAC authorization bypass and HTTP/2
# transport-server denial of service, statically linked into the docker-buildx
# CLI plugin installed by Dockerfile.dev (ARG BUILDX_VERSION). Surfaced only by
# security:trivy:container-scan on the contributor/CI dev image.
#
# Not yet clearable by a pin bump: v0.35.0 remains the latest Buildx release,
# and Buildx master still pins google.golang.org/grpc v1.81.1. The advisory was
# published on 2026-07-21 and fixes all affected versions in gRPC-Go 1.82.1,
# but no Buildx release containing that version exists yet.
#
# Low runtime risk: Buildx runs as a local build-time CLI against a trusted
# BuildKit daemon; it is not deployed as a service and does not expose the
# affected xDS RBAC or HTTP/2 server paths. The dev image is never deployed to
# a cluster.
#
# Clears when a Buildx release ships with google.golang.org/grpc >= 1.82.1:
# bump BUILDX_VERSION in Dockerfile.dev and remove this entry.
# Advisory: https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-hrxh-6v49-42gf
GHSA-hrxh-6v49-42gf exp:2026-09-22

# CVE-2026-14257 (GHSA-mh99-v99m-4gvg) — brace-expansion denial of service via
# unbounded expansion length, causing an out-of-memory process crash. Present in
# the copy npm vendors inside its own node_modules
# (usr/lib/node_modules/npm/node_modules/brace-expansion) in the dev image, so
# it is surfaced only by security:trivy:container-scan on Dockerfile.dev. Fixed
# upstream in brace-expansion 5.0.8.
#
# Not introduced by any change of ours: the advisory was published 2026-07-24
# and reached the Trivy DB after the last green main run, so it appeared on an
# unchanged dev image.
#
# Not clearable by a pin bump: npm 12.0.1 is the latest release (ARG
# NPM_VERSION in Dockerfile.dev) and still bundles brace-expansion 5.0.7. The
# bundled copy lives inside npm's published tarball, where neither
# `npm audit fix` nor an `overrides` entry can reach it.
#
# Low runtime risk: the expansion path is reached through brace globs in npm's
# own CLI argument handling, driven by the contributor or CI invocation rather
# than untrusted remote input. The dev image is a contributor/CI tool and is
# never deployed to a cluster.
#
# Clears when npm ships a release that re-vendors brace-expansion >= 5.0.8:
# bump ARG NPM_VERSION in Dockerfile.dev (plus the packageManager pins the
# consistency check holds in lockstep) and drop this entry.
# Advisory: https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-14257
CVE-2026-14257 exp:2026-08-26

# CVE-2026-56852 — golang.org/x/text, statically linked into two pinned Go
# binaries: the kubectl binary at x/text v0.33.0 (ARG KUBECTL_VERSION in
# Dockerfile.dev; the identical v1.36.3 is fetched by
# lambda/helm-installer/Dockerfile) and the docker-buildx CLI plugin at
# x/text v0.37.0 (ARG BUILDX_VERSION in Dockerfile.dev). Surfaced by
# security:trivy:container-scan on the GCO dev image and the helm-installer
# Lambda image. Fixed in x/text 0.39.0.
#
# Not yet clearable by a pin bump: v1.36.3 is the latest stable kubectl on
# any release line (https://dl.k8s.io/release/stable.txt) and buildx v0.35.0
# is the latest buildx release — no published build of either embeds
# x/text >= 0.39.0 yet.
#
# Low runtime risk: the flaw is a denial-of-service only — norm.Iter enters
# an infinite loop on invalid UTF-8 input (golang/go#80142). kubectl and
# buildx here process operator-authored manifests and build contexts, not
# untrusted remote input, and both images are contributor/CI/deploy tooling
# rather than long-lived network services.
#
# Clears when kubectl and buildx releases ship with x/text >= 0.39.0: bump
# KUBECTL_VERSION and BUILDX_VERSION in Dockerfile.dev and the kubectl pin in
# lambda/helm-installer/Dockerfile + lambda/helm-installer-build/Dockerfile,
# then drop this entry.
# Advisory: https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-56852
CVE-2026-56852 exp:2026-09-28
